1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:05,505
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:11,052 --> 00:00:16,057
<i>The land we're planning to use</i>
<i>is currently occupied by the farmers.</i>

3
00:00:16,141 --> 00:00:18,018
<i>But don't worry, we'll force them out.</i>

4
00:00:18,101 --> 00:00:20,687
[Ivy] <i>What?! I don't want</i>
<i>to be involved in that.</i>

5
00:00:20,770 --> 00:00:22,522
<i>We can't force them out.</i>

6
00:00:22,605 --> 00:00:25,775
-[Diego] <i>What are you doing?</i>
-[cop] <i>We're following orders.</i>

7
00:00:25,859 --> 00:00:27,819
<i>Are you ordered to hurt people, huh?!</i>

8
00:00:27,902 --> 00:00:28,903
<i>Salvage our crops!</i>

9
00:00:29,946 --> 00:00:31,239
<i>We don't need your help!</i>

10
00:00:31,322 --> 00:00:33,324
<i>Don't try to fool the farmers.</i>

11
00:00:33,408 --> 00:00:34,951
<i>You're only after the land, right?!</i>

12
00:00:35,035 --> 00:00:37,078
<i>I just want to help.</i>

13
00:00:37,162 --> 00:00:39,164
<i>You want to help? Then leave Ardiente!</i>

14
00:00:39,247 --> 00:00:41,291
<i>You're smart enough to see that.</i>
<i>And you're beautiful too.</i>

15
00:00:41,374 --> 00:00:43,585
<i>It's a shame you don't have a good heart.</i>

16
00:00:43,668 --> 00:00:45,879
[Jepoy] <i>Someone saw you</i>
<i>destroying the statue.</i>

17
00:00:45,962 --> 00:00:47,839
[Ivy] <i>What?! Who saw me?</i>

18
00:00:47,922 --> 00:00:49,507
[Jepoy] <i>His name is Arthur. He's nuts.</i>

19
00:00:49,591 --> 00:00:50,592
<i>I found these in his house.</i>

20
00:00:50,675 --> 00:00:52,135
[Ivy] <i>These are my father's files.</i>

21
00:00:52,218 --> 00:00:53,887
[Julio] <i>Where is this man right now?</i>

22
00:00:53,970 --> 00:00:55,180
[Dimalanta]<i> He's been detained,</i>
<i>Congressman.</i>

23
00:00:55,263 --> 00:00:57,098
<i>Can you bring him here?</i>

24
00:00:57,182 --> 00:01:01,311
-<i>And burn all the evidence.</i>
-[Dimalanta] <i>Yes, sir.</i>

25
00:01:01,394 --> 00:01:04,898
<i>I thought you'd already silenced that man.</i>

26
00:01:04,981 --> 00:01:09,861
<i>Do you really think a lunatic like him</i>
<i>is capable of doing all this alone?!</i>

27
00:01:10,779 --> 00:01:15,158
[Arthur] <i>The savior has arrived</i>
<i>to destroy you all!</i>

28
00:01:15,241 --> 00:01:17,160
[Arnaldo] <i>No one messes</i>
<i>with my grandfather!</i>

29
00:01:17,243 --> 00:01:18,661
[Diego] <i>Whatever it is you're up to,</i>

30
00:01:18,745 --> 00:01:20,455
<i>I hope you think it over.</i>

31
00:01:20,538 --> 00:01:21,706
[Arnaldo] <i>I'm the mayor. And you?</i>

32
00:01:21,790 --> 00:01:24,000
[Diego] <i>I'm the Ardiente</i>
<i>who cares for the people.</i>

33
00:01:24,083 --> 00:01:25,960
[Ivy] <i>You just need to stand your ground.</i>

34
00:01:26,044 --> 00:01:30,507
<i>Maybe it's time for you to show</i>
<i>that you can play their game,</i>

35
00:01:30,590 --> 00:01:34,803
<i>not as a woman, but as their equal.</i>

36
00:01:39,849 --> 00:01:41,935
[Emilia laughing]

37
00:01:42,936 --> 00:01:44,020
[sighs]

38
00:01:45,271 --> 00:01:47,941
-I better get going.
-[both chuckling]

39
00:01:49,734 --> 00:01:51,152
Thank you, Ivy.

40
00:01:53,488 --> 00:01:55,573
Thank you for all your pieces of advice.

41
00:01:57,158 --> 00:01:58,493
I'll keep them in mind.

42
00:01:59,244 --> 00:02:00,286
Thank you.

43
00:02:02,372 --> 00:02:04,499
Actually, you didn't need my advice.

44
00:02:05,583 --> 00:02:09,796
All you needed was a wake-up call.

45
00:02:13,967 --> 00:02:15,176
Let's go!

46
00:02:15,260 --> 00:02:18,972
-[laughing hysterically]
-[Ivy] Oh!

47
00:02:19,597 --> 00:02:22,517
-[Emilia] I'm really drunk.
-[Ivy chuckling]

48
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:24,227
You know what? Uh…

49
00:02:24,561 --> 00:02:27,105
All right, I'll drive you home.

50
00:02:27,689 --> 00:02:30,692
Aww. Thank you, Ivy.
You're really a good friend.

51
00:02:30,775 --> 00:02:32,026
Thank you!

52
00:02:34,070 --> 00:02:35,113
Thank you.

53
00:02:35,655 --> 00:02:38,408
-Anytime.
-[giggles]

54
00:02:38,491 --> 00:02:41,703
I'm sorry. I'm really drunk.

55
00:02:42,453 --> 00:02:44,831
-So, shall we go?
-[Ivy] Yeah.

56
00:02:56,134 --> 00:02:57,802
[sighs]

57
00:03:10,064 --> 00:03:12,734
<i>Stay away from us!</i>
<i>We don't need your help!</i>

58
00:03:12,817 --> 00:03:15,695
[Ivy] <i>Mr. Torillo, I'm here</i>
<i>because I want to help.</i>

59
00:03:15,778 --> 00:03:16,905
<i>You want to help?!</i>

60
00:03:18,114 --> 00:03:19,574
<i>Then leave Ardiente!</i>

61
00:03:19,782 --> 00:03:23,786
[Julio] <i>I would like</i>
<i>to personally thank Miss Aguas</i>

62
00:03:24,203 --> 00:03:29,000
<i>for her investment</i>
<i>in the export processing zone</i>

63
00:03:29,459 --> 00:03:31,002
<i>in this town.</i>

64
00:03:33,338 --> 00:03:35,632
What is she really here for?

65
00:03:35,715 --> 00:03:38,509
[tense music swelling]

66
00:03:46,184 --> 00:03:48,061
[car revving]

67
00:04:07,163 --> 00:04:11,125
[tense music playing]

68
00:04:32,105 --> 00:04:34,774
[Ivy] <i>I could end your life</i>
<i>right now, Emilia.</i>

69
00:04:35,024 --> 00:04:37,694
<i>But you don't deserve a quick death.</i>

70
00:04:37,902 --> 00:04:41,572
<i>I want you to suffer piece by piece.</i>

71
00:04:45,827 --> 00:04:47,829
[grunting]

72
00:04:48,538 --> 00:04:51,082
[groans loudly]

73
00:04:55,712 --> 00:04:56,796
[gasps]

74
00:04:59,590 --> 00:05:01,134
[gasps and grunts]

75
00:05:02,218 --> 00:05:03,261
Listen to me.

76
00:05:03,970 --> 00:05:05,013
I'll let you escape.

77
00:05:05,388 --> 00:05:07,015
Hide and don't ever come back, okay?

78
00:05:07,098 --> 00:05:08,224
Copy.

79
00:05:15,773 --> 00:05:17,442
[Arnaldo] Hey! Is everything all right?

80
00:05:18,901 --> 00:05:21,195
Make sure that those knots are tight.

81
00:05:21,988 --> 00:05:23,239
-All good, Mayor.
-[grunts]

82
00:05:23,323 --> 00:05:25,116
-[Arnaldo] Good.
-[whimpers]

83
00:05:26,743 --> 00:05:27,785
Put this on him.

84
00:05:30,496 --> 00:05:32,957
[Arthur whimpering] Please, no!

85
00:05:34,751 --> 00:05:36,878
Oh! No need to be scared.

86
00:05:36,961 --> 00:05:39,505
It's your own pack of dynamite.
I'll just use it on you.

87
00:05:39,589 --> 00:05:41,132
[Arthur wailing]

88
00:05:41,215 --> 00:05:43,092
-[Arnaldo] Go on.
-No!

89
00:05:45,219 --> 00:05:47,805
-[Arnaldo chuckling]
-[Arthur gasping]

90
00:05:49,599 --> 00:05:50,641
[Arthur] No!

91
00:05:51,517 --> 00:05:53,102
-[grunts]
-[Arnaldo] Tie it around.

92
00:05:53,186 --> 00:05:55,855
[gasps and whimpers]

93
00:06:03,863 --> 00:06:05,073
-[groans]
-[Arnaldo] You done?

94
00:06:05,615 --> 00:06:07,116
[Arthur wailing]

95
00:06:08,034 --> 00:06:09,077
[Arthur] No!

96
00:06:13,790 --> 00:06:15,833
[Arthur whimpers]

97
00:06:15,917 --> 00:06:17,210
Please don't!

98
00:06:19,754 --> 00:06:20,755
[groans]

99
00:06:21,964 --> 00:06:23,466
-Here, light it up!
-[Arthur] No!

100
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:24,801
No!

101
00:06:24,967 --> 00:06:26,177
-[Arnaldo] Come on.
-No!

102
00:06:27,428 --> 00:06:28,429
[Arthur wails]

103
00:06:29,388 --> 00:06:33,559
[tense music playing]

104
00:06:33,643 --> 00:06:34,685
[grunts]

105
00:06:36,729 --> 00:06:37,688
[gasps]

106
00:06:38,106 --> 00:06:41,025
[tense music playing]

107
00:07:04,298 --> 00:07:05,550
[gunshots]

108
00:07:06,634 --> 00:07:08,136
[gunshots]

109
00:07:09,011 --> 00:07:10,054
[screams]

110
00:07:15,184 --> 00:07:18,938
[gasping]

111
00:07:26,362 --> 00:07:27,947
A lunatic escaped me.

112
00:07:28,531 --> 00:07:29,574
[laughs]

113
00:07:30,283 --> 00:07:32,743
-That lunatic got away!
-[gunshots]

114
00:07:36,706 --> 00:07:38,124
[Jepoy] He won't get that far, Mayor.

115
00:07:38,374 --> 00:07:40,251
With those wounds, he'll be dead soon.

116
00:07:45,047 --> 00:07:46,674
Thanks for saving me back there.

117
00:07:47,717 --> 00:07:49,760
It's my fault. I wasn't careful
around that lunatic.

118
00:07:50,428 --> 00:07:51,721
There's nothing we can do now.

119
00:07:53,097 --> 00:07:54,932
But if the congressman asks…

120
00:07:55,558 --> 00:07:56,934
if I've already dealt with Arthur…

121
00:07:58,561 --> 00:07:59,645
do you know what to say?

122
00:08:00,688 --> 00:08:01,898
You don't have to tell me.

123
00:08:02,732 --> 00:08:04,650
Drive me home. After that…

124
00:08:05,318 --> 00:08:06,569
you can do whatever you want.

125
00:08:10,323 --> 00:08:11,908
[Emilia laughing]

126
00:08:12,533 --> 00:08:13,826
Sorry, Ivy.

127
00:08:13,910 --> 00:08:15,870
-[retches]
-Governor! Oh.

128
00:08:15,953 --> 00:08:18,331
-[Emilia laughing]
-[Ivy] Be careful.

129
00:08:18,873 --> 00:08:21,667
-Let's go here.
-Let's do that again.

130
00:08:21,751 --> 00:08:23,169
[laughing]

131
00:08:23,252 --> 00:08:25,379
-[Ivy] Governor.
-[Julio] Emilia!

132
00:08:25,963 --> 00:08:27,006
[Emilia] Papa.

133
00:08:27,089 --> 00:08:29,592
[Julio] Good evening, Miss Aguas.

134
00:08:30,134 --> 00:08:31,594
[groaning]

135
00:08:31,677 --> 00:08:32,678
Good evening, Congressman.

136
00:08:34,680 --> 00:08:38,851
It looks like my daughter
enjoyed your company.

137
00:08:39,560 --> 00:08:43,773
[sighs] Thank you for driving her home.

138
00:08:45,024 --> 00:08:47,985
I think I can take it from here.

139
00:08:51,322 --> 00:08:53,115
Are you sure, Congressman?

140
00:08:54,534 --> 00:08:55,493
Of course.

141
00:08:55,993 --> 00:08:57,453
She's already home.

142
00:08:57,870 --> 00:08:58,913
I can handle this.

143
00:08:59,789 --> 00:09:00,831
Thank you again.

144
00:09:01,541 --> 00:09:02,583
Thank you.

145
00:09:03,834 --> 00:09:05,711
All right, I'll go ahead.

146
00:09:09,882 --> 00:09:11,259
[Julio] Sit down.

147
00:09:11,926 --> 00:09:13,427
We have to talk.

148
00:09:19,225 --> 00:09:20,560
As always…

149
00:09:21,727 --> 00:09:23,145
-you're not using your brain!
-Ouch!

150
00:09:23,271 --> 00:09:24,438
That hurts, Papa!

151
00:09:24,814 --> 00:09:26,566
-[Julio] You imbecile!
-[Emilia] That hurts.

152
00:09:26,649 --> 00:09:29,819
A woman like you,
getting drunk like that?!

153
00:09:30,319 --> 00:09:33,447
-Show some dignity!
-[grunts]

154
00:09:33,531 --> 00:09:34,407
-Huh!
-[grunts]

155
00:09:34,490 --> 00:09:36,075
[Julio] Use your brain!

156
00:09:36,242 --> 00:09:39,120
Did you forget that you're the governor?

157
00:09:39,203 --> 00:09:42,081
What if the people see you like this?

158
00:09:42,373 --> 00:09:45,167
Do you think they'd respect you, huh?!

159
00:09:45,459 --> 00:09:46,961
-Go inside!
-[Emilia grunts]

160
00:09:47,044 --> 00:09:50,089
Go straight to your room!

161
00:09:50,548 --> 00:09:51,591
[grunts]

162
00:09:51,841 --> 00:09:54,176
-You have no self-respect!
-[grunts]

163
00:09:55,261 --> 00:09:58,431
I don't care about what people say!

164
00:09:58,806 --> 00:09:59,974
[shouting] You are right!

165
00:10:00,057 --> 00:10:03,311
I am the governor,
and I can do anything I want!

166
00:10:03,394 --> 00:10:05,563
[tense music playing]

167
00:10:06,230 --> 00:10:09,609
And when did you learn to talk back?!

168
00:10:10,109 --> 00:10:11,986
You're drunk!

169
00:10:12,236 --> 00:10:14,113
Go inside your--

170
00:10:14,530 --> 00:10:15,573
-Go inside--
-[grunts]

171
00:10:16,240 --> 00:10:18,075
I'm so sick of you!

172
00:10:19,410 --> 00:10:22,371
Stop treating me like a puppet!

173
00:10:22,872 --> 00:10:26,167
Starting now, I am in charge of my life!

174
00:10:28,210 --> 00:10:31,213
[tense music playing]

175
00:10:39,805 --> 00:10:43,809
[romantic music playing]

176
00:10:55,696 --> 00:10:58,282
What are you doing here?
It's already late.

177
00:10:58,741 --> 00:11:01,494
The offices of the executives
are already closed.

178
00:11:03,204 --> 00:11:04,705
I just drove the governor home.

179
00:11:05,539 --> 00:11:08,709
Also, why did you come
to my house earlier?

180
00:11:10,961 --> 00:11:12,129
I wanted to talk to you.

181
00:11:13,756 --> 00:11:15,758
Really? About what?

182
00:11:18,094 --> 00:11:20,137
You know my intentions, Miss Aguas.

183
00:11:21,555 --> 00:11:22,640
But remember this.

184
00:11:24,809 --> 00:11:28,813
I'll do everything in my power
to defend the farmers' rights.

185
00:11:32,274 --> 00:11:33,317
[Julio] Emilia…

186
00:11:34,276 --> 00:11:37,571
since when did you have the guts
to fight back against me?!

187
00:11:39,990 --> 00:11:41,784
[Emilia shouting] I'm so fed up with you!

188
00:11:44,620 --> 00:11:46,163
I'm leaving, Mr. Torillo.

189
00:11:47,748 --> 00:11:52,753
I am an Ardiente!
So treat me like an Ardiente!

190
00:11:53,462 --> 00:11:55,381
I demand your respect!

191
00:11:56,924 --> 00:11:58,342
[Julio] Demand?

192
00:11:58,426 --> 00:12:02,847
You have no right to demand anything!

193
00:12:06,392 --> 00:12:09,103
I will treat you

194
00:12:09,728 --> 00:12:13,399
the way you deserve to be treated.

195
00:12:14,942 --> 00:12:16,944
From the start through till now,

196
00:12:18,612 --> 00:12:23,868
what I see you as is a weak woman.

197
00:12:25,619 --> 00:12:26,579
A fly!

198
00:12:27,371 --> 00:12:29,707
You're just a fly sitting on a cow's back.

199
00:12:29,790 --> 00:12:32,460
So learn to stay in your proper place!

200
00:12:32,543 --> 00:12:34,253
-[Emilia] That's enough!
-[Diego] Grandpa!

201
00:12:38,549 --> 00:12:39,800
Stop it, Grandpa!

202
00:12:48,392 --> 00:12:51,937
Let go, or you'll be punished too!

203
00:12:52,771 --> 00:12:53,814
Let go!

204
00:12:57,318 --> 00:13:00,321
I'm not leaving, and you won't hurt Mom!

205
00:13:01,113 --> 00:13:02,281
[exhales]

206
00:13:04,783 --> 00:13:07,745
Remember this, both of you!

207
00:13:10,206 --> 00:13:11,499
We aren't done here!

208
00:13:20,382 --> 00:13:22,176
Mom, are you okay?

209
00:13:22,343 --> 00:13:27,306
Next time, don't defend me
because I can handle myself!

210
00:13:35,856 --> 00:13:39,151
[Ivy] You should have seen
Julio and Emilia.

211
00:13:39,318 --> 00:13:40,361
[scoffs]

212
00:13:42,196 --> 00:13:44,448
Don't worry, dear.

213
00:13:44,698 --> 00:13:48,410
When this is all over,
and you get your justice,

214
00:13:48,494 --> 00:13:50,663
you can finally tell Diego the truth.

215
00:13:50,829 --> 00:13:52,790
You'll both be free.

216
00:13:53,999 --> 00:13:56,377
I hope when Diego finds the truth…

217
00:13:58,128 --> 00:14:00,381
he'll understand why I did this.

218
00:14:03,425 --> 00:14:05,636
[sighs] Let's not talk about Diego.

219
00:14:08,889 --> 00:14:11,141
How's Jepoy? Any news about him?

220
00:14:11,225 --> 00:14:12,601
He's not answering my calls.

221
00:14:12,685 --> 00:14:16,605
Me too. I've been also trying,
but I can't reach him.

222
00:14:16,689 --> 00:14:18,524
I'm starting to get worried!

223
00:14:19,900 --> 00:14:23,153
[voice prompt] <i>The subscriber</i>
<i>cannot be reached.</i>

224
00:14:23,279 --> 00:14:24,738
<i>Please try again later.</i>

225
00:14:51,098 --> 00:14:53,267
[Ivy] <i>Maybe it's time to show them</i>

226
00:14:53,350 --> 00:14:55,811
<i>that you can play their game…</i>

227
00:14:56,729 --> 00:15:01,400
<i>not as a woman, but as their equal.</i>

228
00:15:02,568 --> 00:15:06,780
<i>As Governor Emilia, and as an Ardiente.</i>

229
00:15:08,324 --> 00:15:10,993
[Emilia] <i>My father's crutches</i>
<i>won't bring me down.</i>

230
00:15:11,994 --> 00:15:13,037
<i>I'm strong.</i>

231
00:15:13,871 --> 00:15:16,290
<i>I'm stronger than before.</i>

232
00:15:16,957 --> 00:15:19,168
<i>I shouldn't get myself hurt.</i>

233
00:15:20,169 --> 00:15:21,962
<i>I can face anything.</i>

234
00:15:25,341 --> 00:15:26,884
[Ivy] He's not answering my calls.

235
00:15:26,967 --> 00:15:28,469
-[Carlotta] Mine too.
-I should go--

236
00:15:28,552 --> 00:15:29,511
[Carlotta] Oh!

237
00:15:30,095 --> 00:15:34,433
[tender music playing]

238
00:15:37,519 --> 00:15:38,771
What happened to you?!

239
00:15:39,063 --> 00:15:42,483
We've been trying to reach you!
Why weren't you answering?!

240
00:15:42,566 --> 00:15:45,903
I-- I couldn't pick up
because my phone broke earlier.

241
00:15:47,529 --> 00:15:49,823
Are you fine? Are you wounded?
Were you hurt?

242
00:15:49,907 --> 00:15:52,242
How are you feeling? Are you fine?

243
00:15:53,494 --> 00:15:55,329
-Jepoy!
-I'm fine.

244
00:15:56,163 --> 00:15:58,082
-I'm perfectly fine.
-[sighs deeply]

245
00:15:59,375 --> 00:16:02,169
-I hope Arthur is also safe.
-Why, what happened to him?

246
00:16:02,252 --> 00:16:03,712
[Jepoy] Arnaldo beat him up.

247
00:16:03,921 --> 00:16:05,005
And even planned to blow Arthur up.

248
00:16:05,089 --> 00:16:07,424
Good thing I let Arthur escape.

249
00:16:08,300 --> 00:16:09,510
Are you sure you're fine?

250
00:16:10,177 --> 00:16:12,763
[tender music playing]

251
00:16:19,770 --> 00:16:22,064
[Emilia] My dear husband is finally home.

252
00:16:23,190 --> 00:16:24,191
[Emilia chuckles softly]

253
00:16:27,194 --> 00:16:30,781
Why are you home so late? You got held up?

254
00:16:30,864 --> 00:16:33,784
[Raul] Yes, because we're out of men.

255
00:16:33,909 --> 00:16:37,746
Tell your dad to hire more men
to make the work--

256
00:16:37,830 --> 00:16:39,498
But you already know

257
00:16:39,581 --> 00:16:42,251
that Papa won't entrust it
to anybody else.

258
00:16:42,334 --> 00:16:44,503
He wants you to manage the business.

259
00:16:44,628 --> 00:16:47,840
It's not easy to manage
the operations alone.

260
00:16:47,923 --> 00:16:49,842
I need more men to help me.

261
00:16:49,925 --> 00:16:51,593
And we need the money,

262
00:16:51,677 --> 00:16:53,220
and you will deliver it to us, right?

263
00:16:53,303 --> 00:16:55,389
Of course, but also talk to your father

264
00:16:55,472 --> 00:16:56,640
so I won't be held up,

265
00:16:56,724 --> 00:16:59,226
and you'll stop nagging me
for coming home late.

266
00:16:59,309 --> 00:17:00,269
It's that easy.

267
00:17:00,352 --> 00:17:02,146
-[Emilia] I know.
-Stop it.

268
00:17:02,646 --> 00:17:05,107
I'm not in the mood. I'm tired, Emilia.

269
00:17:05,190 --> 00:17:07,735
Tired because of work or your mistresses?!

270
00:17:11,238 --> 00:17:12,990
Hold on. What's wrong with you?

271
00:17:13,073 --> 00:17:15,117
Are you all right?
You're acting delirious.

272
00:17:15,200 --> 00:17:17,411
I can smell the cheap perfume
on your skin!

273
00:17:18,620 --> 00:17:19,997
[quietly] She doesn't wear perfume.

274
00:17:20,080 --> 00:17:21,248
What did you say?!

275
00:17:22,666 --> 00:17:24,668
-Nothing--
-[smooches]

276
00:17:24,752 --> 00:17:27,004
[Raul] Emilia, stop.
This isn't funny anymore.

277
00:17:27,087 --> 00:17:28,088
[Emilia yelps]

278
00:17:29,089 --> 00:17:32,801
-What's your problem?
-You are my problem!

279
00:17:33,802 --> 00:17:36,555
All these years, I'm enduring it all!

280
00:17:37,014 --> 00:17:40,100
I enduring all the pain and neglect!

281
00:17:40,476 --> 00:17:42,603
But not this time anymore.

282
00:17:42,936 --> 00:17:45,773
Because you will fulfill
your obligations to me!

283
00:17:46,815 --> 00:17:47,858
[Raul] Stop it!

284
00:17:48,567 --> 00:17:49,860
-Will you stop?!
-[Emilia grunts]

285
00:17:50,611 --> 00:17:51,945
I'm not playing games!

286
00:17:54,114 --> 00:17:55,866
-Raul!
-[slams]

287
00:17:59,369 --> 00:18:01,955
[Ivy] I've decided to hold off
my investment in the Ardientes

288
00:18:02,581 --> 00:18:06,502
so that Arnaldo's project
will be postponed.

289
00:18:09,463 --> 00:18:11,840
They might suspect you because of that.

290
00:18:12,257 --> 00:18:13,300
I know, Jepoy.

291
00:18:15,344 --> 00:18:17,846
That's why we're executing our next move.

292
00:18:18,555 --> 00:18:22,559
It's time to publicly reveal
their true colors.

293
00:18:24,436 --> 00:18:26,897
We've gathered enough evidence.

294
00:18:26,980 --> 00:18:29,566
And don't forget my new friend…

295
00:18:30,567 --> 00:18:32,778
Senator Pablo Alcantara.

296
00:18:33,946 --> 00:18:37,241
I'm sure this issue
will reach the headlines

297
00:18:37,324 --> 00:18:39,368
if his name is involved.

298
00:18:47,167 --> 00:18:48,210
Hmm.

299
00:18:48,794 --> 00:18:49,795
[Jepoy] Thanks.

300
00:18:57,845 --> 00:18:58,887
<i>Later, girls.</i>

301
00:18:59,388 --> 00:19:00,764
<i>Where's the congressman's cut?</i>

302
00:19:00,848 --> 00:19:02,599
[man] <i>Give him the congressman's share!</i>

303
00:19:05,060 --> 00:19:08,480
Who do you think
we should send it to first?

304
00:19:09,022 --> 00:19:11,567
To our friends in the media?

305
00:19:12,526 --> 00:19:14,903
Or to those who attended my party?

306
00:19:16,071 --> 00:19:17,281
Or maybe…

307
00:19:17,364 --> 00:19:18,740
[Raul] <i>Where's the congressman's cut?</i>

308
00:19:19,241 --> 00:19:20,909
…to my closest connections?

309
00:19:26,456 --> 00:19:27,749
It doesn't matter.

310
00:19:28,542 --> 00:19:31,545
When the Ardientes wake up tomorrow…

311
00:19:32,880 --> 00:19:37,259
they're going to face a nightmare.

312
00:19:37,384 --> 00:19:41,805
[tense music playing]

313
00:19:47,019 --> 00:19:49,271
[Julio] How much did you collect, Raul?

314
00:19:51,106 --> 00:19:52,191
Two hundred fifty, Pa.

315
00:19:53,275 --> 00:19:54,276
That's it?

316
00:19:55,777 --> 00:19:57,154
That's the usual amount, isn't it?

317
00:19:57,654 --> 00:20:01,033
But you were gone for two days.

318
00:20:01,658 --> 00:20:03,660
What did you do? Go on vacation…

319
00:20:04,411 --> 00:20:07,331
while we're stuck with our problems here?

320
00:20:09,458 --> 00:20:10,751
Papa, can you please stop?

321
00:20:11,335 --> 00:20:15,380
Raul did his best.
Let's just be thankful to him.

322
00:20:23,347 --> 00:20:25,390
-Raul.
-Yes?

323
00:20:25,807 --> 00:20:26,767
Say something.

324
00:20:28,936 --> 00:20:33,232
Pa, first, the situation there
is not that simple.

325
00:20:34,775 --> 00:20:39,321
That territory belongs
to your political rivals.

326
00:20:39,529 --> 00:20:42,574
Good thing that your friend
in Senate is protecting us.

327
00:20:42,658 --> 00:20:43,784
-[Julio scoffs]
-That's all.

328
00:20:46,328 --> 00:20:47,371
That's the point.

329
00:20:49,623 --> 00:20:52,251
You are protected under my name.

330
00:20:53,085 --> 00:20:56,630
Meaning, you can freely move there.

331
00:20:57,339 --> 00:20:59,466
So, don't give me that lame excuse.

332
00:21:00,384 --> 00:21:01,802
Just admit…

333
00:21:03,220 --> 00:21:06,932
that you had fun
with your cheap women again.

334
00:21:07,015 --> 00:21:08,767
-[clatters]
-Papa, can you please stop?!

335
00:21:09,309 --> 00:21:11,061
I've had enough of this!

336
00:21:11,770 --> 00:21:14,982
Starting today,
only I can chastise my husband!

337
00:21:15,065 --> 00:21:16,984
You have no right
to meddle in our affairs!

338
00:21:17,859 --> 00:21:19,569
[tense music playing]

339
00:21:28,829 --> 00:21:30,789
[maid] Senator, you have a visitor.

340
00:21:33,250 --> 00:21:34,251
-Ah!
-Senator.

341
00:21:34,334 --> 00:21:36,503
Miss Aguas, good morning. Please sit down.

342
00:21:38,422 --> 00:21:43,010
So, what's the problem
that brought you here?

343
00:21:43,969 --> 00:21:45,012
Haven't you heard?

344
00:21:45,095 --> 00:21:47,848
Didn't you receive a video email?

345
00:21:48,640 --> 00:21:51,184
Video? What video?

346
00:21:51,852 --> 00:21:55,522
Senator, I received an email this morning.

347
00:21:56,189 --> 00:21:57,274
I thought it was spam mail,

348
00:21:57,357 --> 00:21:58,734
but when I opened it…

349
00:22:01,403 --> 00:22:02,988
it was a sensitive video.

350
00:22:03,989 --> 00:22:05,407
Now that intrigues me.

351
00:22:06,241 --> 00:22:09,786
Um… Let me check my phone.
It might've slipped my eyes.

352
00:22:13,457 --> 00:22:15,167
[grunting]

353
00:22:19,212 --> 00:22:22,549
This is my house, Emilia!

354
00:22:24,426 --> 00:22:27,012
I will scold anyone I want!

355
00:22:28,180 --> 00:22:31,933
I will chastise anyone I want!

356
00:22:34,061 --> 00:22:35,937
And there's nothing you can do about it.

357
00:22:39,191 --> 00:22:43,779
You will regret
this disrespectful act of yours.

358
00:22:44,905 --> 00:22:47,574
Because this is the last time…

359
00:22:48,450 --> 00:22:49,743
that I tolerate you.

360
00:22:51,495 --> 00:22:53,080
The next time you disrespect me…

361
00:22:56,625 --> 00:22:58,335
I will forget that you're my daughter!

362
00:22:58,418 --> 00:23:00,420
[tense music playing]

363
00:23:15,811 --> 00:23:18,814
Let's enjoy the food. Just let him be.

364
00:23:19,481 --> 00:23:21,233
One day, he'll realize

365
00:23:21,316 --> 00:23:25,445
that anger and vexation
won't solve everything.

366
00:23:26,863 --> 00:23:29,741
One can't force their way
to being relevant.

367
00:23:35,622 --> 00:23:39,167
[tense music playing]

368
00:23:42,796 --> 00:23:44,047
[Raul] <i>Where's the congressman's cut?</i>

369
00:23:44,131 --> 00:23:45,632
[man 1] <i>Give him the congressman's share!</i>

370
00:23:47,551 --> 00:23:48,718
[man 2] <i>This is for the senator.</i>

371
00:23:48,802 --> 00:23:50,178
[man 1] <i>Okay, include that one.</i>

372
00:23:50,512 --> 00:23:52,013
-[Raul] <i>Is this all of it?</i>
-[man 1] <i>Yes, boss.</i>

373
00:23:52,347 --> 00:23:53,265
[indistinct chatter]

374
00:23:53,348 --> 00:23:58,353
[tense music playing]

375
00:24:01,606 --> 00:24:03,817
<i>Are you sure about this, Jepoy?</i>

376
00:24:03,900 --> 00:24:06,027
[Jepoy] <i>Just like the old times.</i>

377
00:24:06,111 --> 00:24:08,113
<i>We both know the risks.</i>

378
00:24:08,905 --> 00:24:09,906
<i>Thank you.</i>

379
00:24:11,366 --> 00:24:13,410
[woman] <i>Who are you doing this for, Jepoy?</i>

380
00:24:13,493 --> 00:24:14,661
<i>You don't have to know.</i>

381
00:24:14,744 --> 00:24:16,288
<i>We're also paying for your silence.</i>

382
00:24:16,788 --> 00:24:18,373
<i>Thanks, then. Until next time.</i>

383
00:24:23,795 --> 00:24:26,840
[tense music swelling]

384
00:24:33,305 --> 00:24:34,764
Where did you get this video?

385
00:24:35,724 --> 00:24:37,851
I just received an email this morning.

386
00:24:38,268 --> 00:24:39,811
I'm sorry, Miss Aguas.

387
00:24:40,812 --> 00:24:42,063
You have to leave now.

388
00:24:46,484 --> 00:24:48,403
Uh… Okay, Senator.

389
00:24:50,864 --> 00:24:52,324
But before I leave…

390
00:24:54,701 --> 00:24:56,411
I have to return this to you.

391
00:24:57,078 --> 00:24:58,496
I can't accept that anymore.

392
00:24:58,580 --> 00:25:01,875
It's the check for the property
you bought at the auction.

393
00:25:03,084 --> 00:25:04,044
Why?

394
00:25:04,961 --> 00:25:06,213
Why?!

395
00:25:06,296 --> 00:25:07,505
Come on, Senator.

396
00:25:08,131 --> 00:25:10,175
I don't want to get involved
in that gambling issue.

397
00:25:10,675 --> 00:25:13,303
For sure, the media will investigate
the source of your funds.

398
00:25:14,679 --> 00:25:16,264
And they might trace that check.

399
00:25:16,890 --> 00:25:20,310
So, you believe that video?

400
00:25:21,353 --> 00:25:25,023
Senator, believe me, I'm trying not to.

401
00:25:25,607 --> 00:25:28,526
But like what you said at the party,
you're close to Congressman.

402
00:25:28,610 --> 00:25:31,821
If the issue spreads,
the media will swarm you,

403
00:25:31,905 --> 00:25:34,783
especially because you passed
the Anti-Gambling Bill.

404
00:25:34,866 --> 00:25:39,788
So, think about what people
will say, Senator.

405
00:25:40,497 --> 00:25:43,959
The senator who authored
the Anti-Gambling Bill

406
00:25:45,585 --> 00:25:47,587
is actually a gambling lord.

407
00:25:51,883 --> 00:25:54,761
[scoffs] Senator, I'm sorry
if this is happening.

408
00:25:56,513 --> 00:25:57,722
I'll get going.

409
00:26:01,351 --> 00:26:02,394
But honestly…

410
00:26:05,272 --> 00:26:07,691
if I were you, I'll distance myself

411
00:26:08,149 --> 00:26:09,192
from Congressman.

412
00:26:12,320 --> 00:26:13,363
Again, I'm sorry.

413
00:26:24,791 --> 00:26:27,502
[tense music playing]

414
00:26:44,311 --> 00:26:46,146
[reporter 1] Good morning, Congressman.

415
00:26:46,229 --> 00:26:47,063
Good morning.

416
00:26:47,147 --> 00:26:48,773
-[reporter 2] Good morning, sir.
-What brings you here?

417
00:26:48,940 --> 00:26:51,484
[reporter 1] We just want
to know your opinion

418
00:26:51,568 --> 00:26:53,069
about the controversial video.

419
00:26:53,153 --> 00:26:55,071
[reporter 2] We just want
to hear your comment.

420
00:26:55,155 --> 00:26:56,072
What video?

421
00:26:56,156 --> 00:26:57,824
About your gambling scandal, sir.

422
00:26:58,283 --> 00:26:59,576
Gambling scandal?!

423
00:27:00,035 --> 00:27:02,787
What are you talking about?!

424
00:27:02,996 --> 00:27:04,122
Here, sir.

425
00:27:08,752 --> 00:27:10,962
-Uh…
-[reporter 1] What can you say?

426
00:27:11,046 --> 00:27:13,882
Is it true that you are a gambling lord?

427
00:27:13,965 --> 00:27:15,925
[Julio] I cannot answer you right now.

428
00:27:16,009 --> 00:27:18,053
-Sir, we'd like to know--
-I have to go to the office.

429
00:27:18,136 --> 00:27:19,721
-Wait, sir.
-We'd like to hear your side…

430
00:27:19,804 --> 00:27:21,306
-[Julio] That's a lie.
-Are you a gambling lord?

431
00:27:21,389 --> 00:27:23,391
-[Julio] No comment.
-[reporter 1] Sir! Congressman!

432
00:27:23,475 --> 00:27:25,185
Just a few words, Congressman!

433
00:27:25,268 --> 00:27:27,103
-I'm sorry!
-We'd like to hear your side.

434
00:27:28,355 --> 00:27:29,314
[suspenseful sting]

435
00:27:31,149 --> 00:27:36,112
[reporter] <i>The family of Solon</i>
<i>Julio Ardiente draws flak</i>

436
00:27:36,196 --> 00:27:40,283
<i>over a viral gambling scandal in his town.</i>

437
00:27:40,367 --> 00:27:42,911
<i>It is believed that Rep. Ardiente himself</i>

438
00:27:42,994 --> 00:27:45,330
<i>is the owner and operator</i>

439
00:27:45,538 --> 00:27:48,792
<i>of the alleged big-time</i>
<i>gambling operation.</i>

440
00:27:48,875 --> 00:27:52,545
<i>Senator Pablo Alcantara,</i>
<i>Rep. Ardiente's close friend,</i>

441
00:27:52,796 --> 00:27:54,881
<i>refused to comment on the issue</i>

442
00:27:54,964 --> 00:27:56,508
<i>as he is also tagged in the scandal.</i>

443
00:27:56,591 --> 00:27:58,843
<i>It can be recalled that Sen. Alcantara</i>

444
00:27:58,927 --> 00:28:01,763
<i>authored the Anti-Gambling Bill</i>
<i>in the Senate.</i>

445
00:28:01,846 --> 00:28:05,934
<i>Now, many are wondering</i>
<i>if both men are working together</i>

446
00:28:06,017 --> 00:28:08,770
<i>in these illegal operations</i>
<i>in Poblacion Ardiente.</i>

447
00:28:16,528 --> 00:28:18,238
Meddling bastards!

448
00:28:19,030 --> 00:28:19,989
[spits]

449
00:28:20,073 --> 00:28:24,369
Arnaldo, have you traced
the source of that email?!

450
00:28:24,661 --> 00:28:27,455
Not yet. Our men are having
a hard time decrypting it.

451
00:28:28,415 --> 00:28:32,127
Emilia, have you contacted Senator Pablo?

452
00:28:32,419 --> 00:28:33,920
I've been trying to call him,

453
00:28:34,003 --> 00:28:35,004
but he is not answering.

454
00:28:35,088 --> 00:28:36,589
It looks like he's avoiding us!

455
00:28:36,673 --> 00:28:39,050
His secretary told me
that the senator is busy.

456
00:28:39,718 --> 00:28:40,719
Coward!

457
00:28:42,303 --> 00:28:43,930
Damn it! You're all useless!

458
00:28:44,597 --> 00:28:47,517
Don't blame this on us, Papa!
It's not our fault!

459
00:28:49,436 --> 00:28:52,230
Arnaldo, contact the press.

460
00:28:52,564 --> 00:28:56,025
I need to get to the media first
before Pablo does.

461
00:28:56,234 --> 00:28:57,736
I have to contain this!

462
00:28:58,778 --> 00:28:59,779
A press conference?!

463
00:29:00,155 --> 00:29:03,408
Papa, a press conference
won't do you good!

464
00:29:03,742 --> 00:29:04,701
What will you do?!

465
00:29:04,784 --> 00:29:07,120
You will deny the video?! You will lie?!

466
00:29:08,037 --> 00:29:08,997
Come on!

467
00:29:09,080 --> 00:29:12,792
Papa, the best way to handle
things is to keep quiet!

468
00:29:12,959 --> 00:29:14,586
Less talk, less mistakes!

469
00:29:16,588 --> 00:29:19,090
-[Loring] Diego! Diego!
-[Diego] What is it?

470
00:29:19,174 --> 00:29:20,133
Something happened!

471
00:29:20,216 --> 00:29:22,010
The reporters are saying
that your grandfather

472
00:29:22,510 --> 00:29:24,679
is a gambling lord!

473
00:29:24,763 --> 00:29:25,847
[man] Is that true, Diego?

474
00:29:25,930 --> 00:29:29,434
Everyone is innocent until proven guilty.

475
00:29:30,185 --> 00:29:32,645
We shouldn't believe in rumors.

476
00:29:33,146 --> 00:29:36,024
But don't worry,
I'll get to the bottom of this.

477
00:29:39,819 --> 00:29:41,112
[laughs]

478
00:29:41,279 --> 00:29:42,572
Terrific!

479
00:29:42,906 --> 00:29:44,365
What would you like to happen?!

480
00:29:44,783 --> 00:29:47,410
Do you want to ruin my reputation?!

481
00:29:47,744 --> 00:29:48,995
Are you nuts?!

482
00:29:50,163 --> 00:29:51,956
No! I will speak up!

483
00:29:52,916 --> 00:29:56,920
And besides, I know
how to handle these things.

484
00:29:57,003 --> 00:30:01,591
You have no right to dictate my decisions!

485
00:30:02,509 --> 00:30:04,594
Arnaldo, contact the press.

486
00:30:05,011 --> 00:30:06,054
Copy that.

487
00:30:06,930 --> 00:30:08,223
Raul, you moron!

488
00:30:09,808 --> 00:30:12,727
Don't you dare leave this house!

489
00:30:14,020 --> 00:30:16,606
This is all your fault!

490
00:30:16,689 --> 00:30:18,107
[tense music playing]

491
00:30:18,191 --> 00:30:19,859
I will deal with you later.

492
00:30:20,777 --> 00:30:22,612
Good-for-nothing people!

493
00:30:30,203 --> 00:30:34,165
A good and honest politician

494
00:30:34,624 --> 00:30:37,585
does not hide anything
from his constituents.

495
00:30:37,669 --> 00:30:42,090
That is why I chose to face you
and to tell you honestly

496
00:30:42,298 --> 00:30:44,509
that the viral video

497
00:30:45,343 --> 00:30:48,388
involving me in a gambling scandal

498
00:30:48,763 --> 00:30:50,348
is not true.

499
00:30:50,640 --> 00:30:52,892
It was fabricated by people…

500
00:30:54,185 --> 00:30:55,812
who want to ruin

501
00:30:56,145 --> 00:30:59,399
my long and clean record
in public service.

502
00:30:59,649 --> 00:31:01,234
So, now…

503
00:31:02,485 --> 00:31:06,155
I am apologizing…

504
00:31:06,990 --> 00:31:09,909
to every citizen of Poblacion Ardiente.

505
00:31:10,785 --> 00:31:14,289
I apologize because
I let these people ruin…

506
00:31:14,372 --> 00:31:16,207
[Loring] Diego, I know you said

507
00:31:16,291 --> 00:31:19,002
that everyone is innocent
until proven guilty.

508
00:31:19,085 --> 00:31:20,503
But what do you think about this?

509
00:31:20,587 --> 00:31:22,046
[Diego] I don't know anything about this.

510
00:31:22,130 --> 00:31:24,090
But I think everyone…

511
00:31:25,508 --> 00:31:28,261
wants to believe in
the innocence of their family.

512
00:31:28,344 --> 00:31:30,930
This is the first time I've seen
your grandfather like that.

513
00:31:31,180 --> 00:31:34,017
He looks weak and aging.

514
00:31:34,100 --> 00:31:36,853
I'll be worried if he starts
looking younger.

515
00:31:36,936 --> 00:31:37,979
[Pandoy laughing]

516
00:31:38,062 --> 00:31:39,772
[Loring] Come on, Pandoy.
There you go again!

517
00:31:39,856 --> 00:31:42,150
You know what I mean!

518
00:31:43,776 --> 00:31:46,779
I'm sure Grandpa is furious
with Dad again.

519
00:31:47,447 --> 00:31:48,990
[reporter 1] But how do you explain

520
00:31:49,073 --> 00:31:51,576
that your name is mentioned in the video?

521
00:31:51,784 --> 00:31:53,328
[Julio chuckles] Come on.

522
00:31:54,037 --> 00:31:58,249
We all know how advanced
technology is nowadays.

523
00:31:58,333 --> 00:32:02,211
The voice on the video could
have been tampered with.

524
00:32:02,295 --> 00:32:04,839
[reporter 2]
Let's say the audio was edited.

525
00:32:04,923 --> 00:32:06,341
But how can you explain

526
00:32:06,424 --> 00:32:09,093
the presence of Raul Torillo
in the footage?

527
00:32:09,177 --> 00:32:10,803
You know, my friends…

528
00:32:12,805 --> 00:32:15,683
not all families are perfect.

529
00:32:15,767 --> 00:32:19,938
Mr. Raul Torillo has a gambling problem,

530
00:32:20,021 --> 00:32:23,232
and we just found out recently.

531
00:32:23,524 --> 00:32:30,490
The governor and her husband
are working on this problem.

532
00:32:30,865 --> 00:32:35,161
Don't worry, it won't take long
until things return to normal.

533
00:32:35,578 --> 00:32:38,665
[reporter 1]
Can we talk to Mr. Raul Torillo?

534
00:32:38,790 --> 00:32:39,832
Where is he?

535
00:32:39,958 --> 00:32:46,798
[Julio] Uh… They asked
that we respect their privacy

536
00:32:46,965 --> 00:32:51,135
while they are coping with this situation.

537
00:32:51,386 --> 00:32:53,304
[reporter 1] Drop the act, Congressman.

538
00:32:53,638 --> 00:32:57,183
Present Mister Torillo.
We know you're hiding him.

539
00:32:57,517 --> 00:32:58,851
[reporter 2] Yes, Congressman.

540
00:32:59,227 --> 00:33:01,396
We need Mr. Torillo's statement
to validate all this.

541
00:33:01,479 --> 00:33:04,023
[reporter 3] Are you hiding Mr. Torillo?

542
00:33:04,107 --> 00:33:04,983
Why is that, Congressman?

543
00:33:05,066 --> 00:33:07,360
[reporter 4] Is it true that you
have problems with Mr. Torillo?

544
00:33:07,652 --> 00:33:09,612
[reporter 5] Is there a conflict
between you and Mr. Torillo?

545
00:33:12,031 --> 00:33:12,949
Okay, that's it!

546
00:33:13,032 --> 00:33:14,784
That's it! That ends our press conference.

547
00:33:14,867 --> 00:33:17,036
Thank you so much for coming.
You may now leave.

548
00:33:17,120 --> 00:33:18,955
-Thank you.
-Thank you, everyone.

549
00:33:23,793 --> 00:33:25,253
-[Emilia] Papa.
-Hands off me!

550
00:33:28,006 --> 00:33:30,091
This is you and your husband's fault!

551
00:33:30,842 --> 00:33:31,884
[exhales]

552
00:33:32,927 --> 00:33:36,139
Papa! Why are you all
blaming this on Raul?!

553
00:33:36,222 --> 00:33:37,724
He isn't solely responsible for this.

554
00:33:37,807 --> 00:33:40,893
I told you this press conference
won't do you any good,

555
00:33:40,977 --> 00:33:42,437
but you still pushed through!

556
00:33:42,770 --> 00:33:44,313
Emilia, I can't…

557
00:33:44,772 --> 00:33:46,858
-Help your grandfather!
-[Ivy] Congressman.

558
00:33:48,067 --> 00:33:49,110
[Emilia] My god!

559
00:33:49,902 --> 00:33:51,320
Can you please take him to his room?

560
00:33:51,404 --> 00:33:54,365
-[Julio] Arnaldo, come with me.
-[Arnaldo] Of course.

561
00:34:00,872 --> 00:34:01,956
Is he okay?

562
00:34:02,623 --> 00:34:04,042
[Emilia] Have you been there all long?

563
00:34:04,250 --> 00:34:06,127
Uh… No, I just arrived.

564
00:34:06,669 --> 00:34:08,296
I came as soon as I heard.

565
00:34:08,921 --> 00:34:09,964
How's the situation?

566
00:34:10,131 --> 00:34:12,175
[sighs] It's bad. It's really bad.

567
00:34:12,258 --> 00:34:14,343
Everything is just taking a toll on Papa.

568
00:34:14,427 --> 00:34:16,220
He won't listen to me.

569
00:34:17,430 --> 00:34:20,308
But you know, I just have to thank you

570
00:34:20,391 --> 00:34:21,601
that you urged me to speak up.

571
00:34:21,684 --> 00:34:25,396
At least, I proved to myself
that my opinions are valid.

572
00:34:25,480 --> 00:34:27,440
Papa just won't listen to me.

573
00:34:27,523 --> 00:34:30,985
If he had listened to me,
this wouldn't have happened.

574
00:34:35,156 --> 00:34:38,242
Governor, if you need someone to talk to,

575
00:34:38,618 --> 00:34:39,660
I'm just here.

576
00:34:40,787 --> 00:34:43,331
Thank you, Ivy. Thank you.

577
00:34:49,962 --> 00:34:52,548
[Emilia] Looks like that lunatic
was right,

578
00:34:52,632 --> 00:34:54,675
that the Ardiente household will fall!

579
00:34:55,093 --> 00:34:56,844
Our empire is falling!

580
00:34:57,470 --> 00:34:59,180
And I need to save it.

581
00:35:01,140 --> 00:35:04,143
[sighs] Governor, why not ask for help?

582
00:35:04,227 --> 00:35:05,937
Isn't the senator involved in this?

583
00:35:06,020 --> 00:35:08,898
Ivy, please stop calling me "Governor"!

584
00:35:08,981 --> 00:35:09,941
Emilia will do.

585
00:35:10,024 --> 00:35:12,527
-Fine.
-And that Senator is another problem.

586
00:35:12,610 --> 00:35:14,445
He won't answer our calls!

587
00:35:14,529 --> 00:35:17,782
He knows this will backfire on all of us!

588
00:35:18,825 --> 00:35:19,826
You know,

589
00:35:20,493 --> 00:35:22,787
this is so frustrating!

590
00:35:24,705 --> 00:35:26,874
Emilia, relax.

591
00:35:26,958 --> 00:35:30,503
For sure, you can manage.
You'll find a way.

592
00:35:35,508 --> 00:35:37,635
[sighs] Relax, okay?

593
00:35:38,761 --> 00:35:40,721
I think I found a solution.

594
00:35:40,805 --> 00:35:41,889
I see.

595
00:35:42,932 --> 00:35:45,184
And I'm looking at her now.

596
00:35:45,977 --> 00:35:47,270
What?

597
00:35:47,353 --> 00:35:49,188
Me? Emilia!

598
00:35:49,272 --> 00:35:51,149
Ivy, wait!

599
00:35:51,232 --> 00:35:54,026
All you got to do
is just vouch for our name.

600
00:35:54,110 --> 00:35:55,736
Just tell the public

601
00:35:55,820 --> 00:35:57,155
that the Ardientes are good people.

602
00:35:57,238 --> 00:35:59,240
That's why you're still investing in us.

603
00:35:59,323 --> 00:36:02,785
-But Emilia, you know that--
-Ivy! Hear me out, okay?

604
00:36:02,869 --> 00:36:04,203
Hear me out.

605
00:36:04,287 --> 00:36:06,289
Just prove to everyone

606
00:36:06,372 --> 00:36:09,083
that the Ardientes are good people,

607
00:36:09,167 --> 00:36:10,626
that we are innocent.

608
00:36:10,710 --> 00:36:13,462
You know, for somebody like you
who's got a stellar reputation,

609
00:36:13,546 --> 00:36:15,047
people will listen!

610
00:36:15,131 --> 00:36:17,216
But you are innocent, right?

611
00:36:17,758 --> 00:36:19,468
The video is not true, right?

612
00:36:20,928 --> 00:36:22,096
Tell me.

613
00:36:26,434 --> 00:36:27,435
Emilia…

614
00:36:33,733 --> 00:36:34,817
Ivy.

615
00:36:40,239 --> 00:36:42,658
-You are my friend, right?
-Yes.

616
00:36:42,742 --> 00:36:45,786
-I can trust you.
-Yes, Emilia.

617
00:36:45,870 --> 00:36:47,830
That's why I'm going
to tell you the truth.

618
00:36:50,750 --> 00:36:51,792
Ivy…

619
00:36:53,294 --> 00:36:56,756
the video and the accusations against us…

620
00:36:59,050 --> 00:37:00,134
are all true.

621
00:37:03,471 --> 00:37:04,805
[Emilia sighs]

622
00:37:04,889 --> 00:37:06,766
Now that you know the truth,

623
00:37:09,101 --> 00:37:10,519
will you still help us?

624
00:37:22,490 --> 00:37:23,699
How are you feeling?

625
00:37:28,663 --> 00:37:30,539
I've been worse.

626
00:37:31,332 --> 00:37:33,668
Don't worry, I'm fine.

627
00:37:35,503 --> 00:37:36,921
I'll be okay…

628
00:37:38,172 --> 00:37:42,218
as long as Raul doesn't show his face!

629
00:37:43,719 --> 00:37:45,221
And your mother…

630
00:37:46,764 --> 00:37:49,100
she's another headache.

631
00:37:50,434 --> 00:37:54,480
I don't understand why of all times,

632
00:37:54,563 --> 00:37:59,402
she chose to go against me now.

633
00:37:59,986 --> 00:38:01,070
Calm down, Grandpa.

634
00:38:02,780 --> 00:38:03,781
I will fix this.

635
00:38:04,824 --> 00:38:06,617
<i>We </i>will fix this.

636
00:38:08,744 --> 00:38:11,372
I'll talk to my parents and track down

637
00:38:12,039 --> 00:38:14,709
whoever is messing with the Ardientes.

638
00:38:15,626 --> 00:38:18,921
And I promise to make them pay.

639
00:38:20,798 --> 00:38:23,551
I appreciate your honesty, Emilia.

640
00:38:24,802 --> 00:38:26,721
At least, I know now…

641
00:38:27,430 --> 00:38:30,057
with whom I'm trusting my money.

642
00:38:33,060 --> 00:38:35,896
So, are you staying?

643
00:38:37,690 --> 00:38:39,150
Are you pursuing your investment?

644
00:38:46,699 --> 00:38:49,368
Thank you, Ivy! Thank you.

645
00:38:51,287 --> 00:38:52,288
[exhales sharply]

646
00:38:53,080 --> 00:38:55,791
[tense music playing]

647
00:39:04,884 --> 00:39:06,635
All my life,
you have prepared me for this,

648
00:39:06,719 --> 00:39:07,803
and I'll prove to you

649
00:39:07,887 --> 00:39:10,389
that everything you taught me
will not go to waste.

650
00:39:11,932 --> 00:39:14,894
Spoken like a true Ardiente.

651
00:39:15,978 --> 00:39:17,104
You know, Arnaldo…

652
00:39:17,688 --> 00:39:21,067
I'm grateful to have someone like you…

653
00:39:22,068 --> 00:39:25,237
that I can depend on
in situations like this.

654
00:39:27,156 --> 00:39:28,407
When I'm gone…

655
00:39:29,950 --> 00:39:32,286
all this will be yours.

656
00:39:34,330 --> 00:39:39,502
You will be the king
of Poblacion Ardiente.

657
00:39:41,003 --> 00:39:43,464
Take good care of our name.

658
00:39:46,759 --> 00:39:47,843
I will not disappoint you.

659
00:39:59,397 --> 00:40:00,439
-Dad!
-[Raul] Hey.

660
00:40:01,148 --> 00:40:02,149
Son!

661
00:40:03,150 --> 00:40:05,778
Join me for a drink.
It's boring to be alone.

662
00:40:07,071 --> 00:40:09,073
-You're not drinking alone.
-Why?

663
00:40:09,490 --> 00:40:12,159
Those mosquitoes
are also chugging your blood.

664
00:40:13,160 --> 00:40:14,870
That's what I like about you, son.

665
00:40:15,454 --> 00:40:17,373
It's good you have a sense of humor.

666
00:40:17,498 --> 00:40:22,294
Those people inside?
All they do is get mad.

667
00:40:22,461 --> 00:40:24,755
They're all angry, especially with me.

668
00:40:26,757 --> 00:40:28,259
Is that why you're outside?

669
00:40:29,260 --> 00:40:30,302
[clicks tongue]

670
00:40:31,303 --> 00:40:33,139
I've always been outside, son.

671
00:40:34,056 --> 00:40:36,016
I've always been alone outside…

672
00:40:36,809 --> 00:40:39,311
because this family never accepted me.

673
00:40:42,815 --> 00:40:43,983
Welcome to the club.

674
00:40:48,237 --> 00:40:49,280
You really are my son.

675
00:40:49,780 --> 00:40:51,282
I saw the video.

676
00:40:52,032 --> 00:40:53,742
I don't want to talk about that.

677
00:40:54,243 --> 00:40:57,037
-But, Dad--
-I don't want to talk about it.

678
00:40:59,290 --> 00:41:01,792
Give me a break, will you?

679
00:41:03,002 --> 00:41:06,046
If you don't want to join me, that's fine.

680
00:41:07,214 --> 00:41:08,382
Just go inside.

681
00:41:17,183 --> 00:41:19,143
[Emilia on voice memo]
<i>I'm going to tell you the truth.</i>

682
00:41:19,226 --> 00:41:20,269
<i>Ivy…</i>

683
00:41:21,479 --> 00:41:25,900
<i>the video and the accusations</i>
<i>against us are all true.</i>

684
00:41:27,568 --> 00:41:29,028
<i>Now that you know the truth…</i>

685
00:41:30,654 --> 00:41:32,198
<i>will you still help us?</i>

686
00:41:32,740 --> 00:41:35,743
[tense music playing]

687
00:41:51,091 --> 00:41:54,803
The Ardiente's downfall is within reach.

688
00:41:55,095 --> 00:41:59,016
[tense music playing]

689
00:41:59,642 --> 00:42:00,434
[beeps]

690
00:42:08,484 --> 00:42:09,527
Hey, Diego!

691
00:42:10,778 --> 00:42:12,029
Glad to see you home.

692
00:42:12,863 --> 00:42:16,116
I thought you'd joined
the critics of Grandpa.

693
00:42:16,992 --> 00:42:19,995
Even though you do things
that I can hardly swallow…

694
00:42:21,539 --> 00:42:22,581
I still love you all.

695
00:42:23,541 --> 00:42:26,544
And I'll keep you all
out of trouble if I have to.

696
00:42:31,799 --> 00:42:32,841
Papa.

697
00:42:34,677 --> 00:42:37,263
-How are you feeling?
-I'm fine.

698
00:42:38,764 --> 00:42:44,436
I've already taken my medicines.
Now, I need to rest.

699
00:42:44,645 --> 00:42:47,523
Do you want a nurse to look after you?

700
00:42:47,606 --> 00:42:48,566
Emilia.

701
00:42:49,984 --> 00:42:52,278
Why are you being like this?

702
00:42:53,571 --> 00:42:58,242
Why are you becoming a thorn in my side?!

703
00:42:58,909 --> 00:43:00,286
What do you want?

704
00:43:00,369 --> 00:43:02,162
Are you trying to prove something?

705
00:43:02,246 --> 00:43:05,249
It's like you're trying to prove
that you can manage,

706
00:43:05,457 --> 00:43:08,627
that you're already better
than me, is that it?

707
00:43:08,711 --> 00:43:11,046
No. That we are equal, Papa!

708
00:43:11,213 --> 00:43:13,882
That being a woman doesn't mean
I'm weaker than you.

709
00:43:14,049 --> 00:43:15,092
Oh!

710
00:43:19,346 --> 00:43:25,394
Women were created to be servants of men!

711
00:43:26,312 --> 00:43:31,233
Don't wait for me to put you
in your proper place, Emilia!

712
00:43:38,741 --> 00:43:39,908
Okay, that's good.

713
00:43:41,035 --> 00:43:43,704
I'm expecting your help
to resolve our family problem.

714
00:43:45,539 --> 00:43:46,790
Arnaldo, don't you think…

715
00:43:47,875 --> 00:43:50,377
it's time for our family to change?

716
00:43:51,003 --> 00:43:53,547
Let's turn away from these illegal things.

717
00:43:54,840 --> 00:43:55,966
I'm not blind, Arnaldo.

718
00:43:56,800 --> 00:43:58,052
I know the business of this family.

719
00:43:58,135 --> 00:43:59,678
I know what's going on in this house.

720
00:43:59,762 --> 00:44:02,598
I chose to keep quiet because I believe
that you can change--

721
00:44:02,681 --> 00:44:04,725
We don't have to change anything, Diego.

722
00:44:05,267 --> 00:44:06,101
Nothing.

723
00:44:06,518 --> 00:44:09,188
We rule this town
because we have the power!

724
00:44:10,564 --> 00:44:14,193
I don't understand
why you still can't grasp that.

725
00:44:16,362 --> 00:44:20,240
In Ardiente, we are the rulers!

726
00:44:29,750 --> 00:44:31,001
[Julio laughs]

727
00:44:31,251 --> 00:44:34,797
Your faithful husband is finally here!

728
00:44:35,798 --> 00:44:39,218
Do you see the consequences
of your actions?

729
00:44:40,761 --> 00:44:46,558
Did you see how the media
disrespected me because of you?!

730
00:44:46,642 --> 00:44:49,478
That wouldn't be the case
if you answered better.

731
00:44:52,439 --> 00:44:54,983
Now you're also talking back, huh?!

732
00:44:55,526 --> 00:44:57,694
-Have you forgotten--
-[Raul] I haven't forgotten.

733
00:44:57,778 --> 00:45:00,030
That's why I'm telling you to also stop!

734
00:45:00,114 --> 00:45:01,782
[Emilia] Raul, stop. That's enough!

735
00:45:02,866 --> 00:45:04,284
[Julio laughing] Hey!

736
00:45:05,369 --> 00:45:08,163
Go on! That's what you're good at!

737
00:45:08,247 --> 00:45:10,916
Running after picking a fight,

738
00:45:10,999 --> 00:45:15,170
and then hiding behind your wife.

739
00:45:15,254 --> 00:45:19,341
Yes! Just let your wife save you again

740
00:45:19,425 --> 00:45:21,844
from another one of your failures!

741
00:45:21,927 --> 00:45:23,387
Oh, Raul.

742
00:45:23,470 --> 00:45:25,639
It doesn't surprise me anymore

743
00:45:25,722 --> 00:45:28,725
because you are that kind of man!

744
00:45:29,435 --> 00:45:36,024
You are a good-for-nothing son of a--

745
00:45:36,108 --> 00:45:40,362
[Julio grunting]

746
00:45:40,446 --> 00:45:42,656
-[Raul] I'll kill you, bastard!
-[Julio grunting]

747
00:45:42,739 --> 00:45:44,950
What are you doing, Raul?!

748
00:45:45,033 --> 00:45:46,869
-[Raul growls]
-Stop it, Raul!

749
00:45:46,952 --> 00:45:48,912
-[Raul] I'll kill you!
-Raul, stop it!

750
00:45:49,788 --> 00:45:52,958
Raul, what are you doing?! Stop it! Stop!

751
00:45:53,709 --> 00:45:55,544
-[Raul] What now?!
-[Emilia] Stop it!

752
00:45:56,086 --> 00:45:57,588
[both grunting]

753
00:45:57,671 --> 00:45:58,714
[Emilia] Papa!

754
00:46:02,593 --> 00:46:04,011
Papa!

755
00:46:04,094 --> 00:46:05,262
Papa!

756
00:46:05,804 --> 00:46:08,640
Papa? [crying]

757
00:46:10,142 --> 00:46:12,519
[wailing] Papa!

758
00:46:13,312 --> 00:46:14,771
Papa!

759
00:46:16,857 --> 00:46:19,693
Papa!

760
00:46:23,447 --> 00:46:24,781
[Emilia] <i>My time has come.</i>

761
00:46:24,865 --> 00:46:27,701
<i>Now that the king is gone,</i>
<i>I shall reign as the queen.</i>

762
00:46:27,784 --> 00:46:28,827
[Diego] <i>I've just noticed.</i>

763
00:46:28,911 --> 00:46:30,787
<i>Whenever something bad</i>
<i>happens to my family,</i>

764
00:46:30,871 --> 00:46:31,830
<i>you're always there.</i>

765
00:46:31,914 --> 00:46:35,000
<i>Why are you so concerned about my family?</i>

766
00:46:35,083 --> 00:46:37,878
[Ivy] <i>You shouldn't get dragged</i>
<i>into this, Diego.</i>

767
00:46:37,961 --> 00:46:40,172
<i>But if you get in my way,</i>

768
00:46:40,255 --> 00:46:42,424
<i>I'll have no choice</i>
<i>but to deal with you too.</i>

769
00:46:42,508 --> 00:46:44,009
[Raul] <i>You know, Emilia, if you think</i>

770
00:46:44,092 --> 00:46:47,721
<i>you can leash me forever,</i>
<i>then you are wrong.</i>

771
00:46:47,804 --> 00:46:48,764
<i>I won't let you do that.</i>

772
00:46:48,847 --> 00:46:50,807
[Emilia] <i>On the contrary,</i>
<i>I don't want you here.</i>

773
00:46:50,891 --> 00:46:53,685
<i>You can stay with your relatives</i>
<i>if you still have any.</i>

774
00:46:53,769 --> 00:46:55,604
[Raul] <i>Love, I'm back.</i>

775
00:46:55,687 --> 00:46:59,399
[theme music playing]
